    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know there are numbers to call. but they dont get it. they just try to pull you back to the surface where it's all loud and exhausting again. i'm not looking for a way to fix the weight, i'm just looking for the quiet. the quiet that comes when you stop pretending you're supposed to be here. doesn't it seem logical? to just stop resisting the pull of the void? it like only real left. maybe honest, dont",
